phi-adapter-onkyo (0.0~git202609081042.8cb7ec9-1) trixie; urgency=medium

  * A query is answered when its own answer arrives, not when any frame does,
    and the next one goes out at that moment. The fixed 120 ms wait after each
    answer is gone: four instant answers took 482 ms and now take none, and on
    a measured Pioneer - which answers each query with one frame and volunteers
    nothing - it was 480 ms of a 1048 ms poll.
  * A query a model does not know is counted and skipped instead of failing the
    exchange, so the other three answers still arrive. Only a receiver that has
    answered nothing at all is given up on, after one timeout rather than four.

 -- Marius Schumacher <marius.schumacher@phisys.com>  Tue, 08 Sep 2026 10:42:55 +0200

